<div class="main-title">Likutay Halachos &mdash; Choshen Mishpat II</div>
<div class="sub-title">Hilchos Shomer Sachar<br>[Laws of a Paid Guardian]</div>
<div class="sub-sub">And in it will be explained the matter of Chanukah</div>

<div class="halacha-title">Halacha 2 &mdash; Part C (&sect;&sect;11&ndash;16)</div>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;11</div>

<p>And in each and every generation there is found such a Tzaddik who knows how to walk toward the spirit and the ratzon of each and every one &mdash; through whom peace would be made in the world. And through this, everyone would return to Hashem, blessed be He, for everything depends on peace, as is explained elsewhere. For through the peace, one can draw the entire world to His service. For through the peace, which is the aspect of ratzon and love and unity, through this they are incorporated in the one Supernal Ratzon, and all the forces of the Evil Inclination are nullified &mdash; whose sustenance is from the aspect of the variation of r&rsquo;tzonos, from which it draws sustenance and introduces heresies and dispute. For the Evil Inclination is called &ldquo;dispute.&rdquo; And the nullification of the Evil Inclination is through the peace. And therefore peace is very great, as our Sages of blessed memory expounded extensively in many places.</p>

<p>But when the Evil One sees that such a Tzaddik is found, who is in the aspect of ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin, who can make peace among all &mdash; then he stirs up a great dispute against this great Tzaddik himself, until everyone disputes against him more than against anyone else in the world. For in truth, everyone is distant from him. For each person is distant from his fellow because of the variation of the r&rsquo;tzonos between him and his fellow &mdash; because he does not believe that both r&rsquo;tzonos are included in one at their root. But the variation and the distance between a person and his fellow is very small, for in most of their ways they are alike in their desires and their traits &mdash; there is only some distance and variation between them.</p>

<p>But from this great Tzaddik, everyone is completely distant. For he is exalted and uplifted above all the variation of the r&rsquo;tzonos of all people in the world. For he is completely distant from the entire world, and he has no desire for this world at all. He is only always incorporated in the Supernal Ratzon, in the aspect of ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin. And one who believes in him and draws close to him &mdash; then each and every one can find himself within this Tzaddik. For he is the root of the souls of Israel and is comprised of all of them. For he is in the aspect of the Ratzon of the R&rsquo;tzonos &mdash; that is, the Supernal Ratzon that is clothed in all the r&rsquo;tzonos and the souls of all people in the world.</p>

<p>But when the Evil One introduces heresies and dispute into the hearts of people, to divide their hearts from him, then the dispute against him is greater than all other types of dispute &mdash; because he is distant and exalted from all the r&rsquo;tzonos of all who come into the world, who all have variations among them, while he has no variation of desire for this world at all. And therefore everyone disputes against him and cannot bear him.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the dispute of the Sh&rsquo;vatim [tribes] against Yosef HaTzaddik. For Yosef HaTzaddik is the aspect of this Tzaddik mentioned above, the aspect of ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin, the aspect of Moshe. For Yosef, Moshe, and Dovid are all one aspect &mdash; for all three departed on Shabbos at Minchah, at ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin.</p>

<p>And all the holy Sh&rsquo;vatim, even though they were all great and awesome tzadikim &mdash; even so, they all needed to be connected to him. And this is the aspect of the connection of all the r&rsquo;tzonos to the root of the Ratzon, which is the aspect of the holy elder, which is the aspect of Yosef HaTzaddik, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;For he was the son of his old age&rdquo;</span> [ben z&rsquo;kunim] <span class="inline-source">(Beraishis 37:3)</span> &mdash; &ldquo;son of old age&rdquo; specifically &mdash; whose root is in the aspect of the holy elder, which is the aspect of the maitzach haratzon, the aspect of ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of what Yosef told them his dream: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And behold, we were binding sheaves in the field, and behold, my sheaf arose,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;and behold, your sheaves surrounded and bowed down to my sheaf&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Beraishis 37:7)</span>. For all the Sh&rsquo;vatim, who are the totality of Israel, bind knots and unify unifications &mdash; which is the aspect of the connection of the r&rsquo;tzonos together. But all the knots and unifications need to come to the Tzaddik of the generation, who is the aspect of Yosef &mdash; who is the aspect of ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin, who connects all the knots and the unifications to the Supernal Ratzon, in the aspect of: &ldquo;and behold, your sheaves surrounded and bowed down to my sheaf.&rdquo;</p>

<p>And therefore the dream was regarding the labor of the field. For the rectification of the labor of the field is through the illumination of the Ratzon, through which all the thirty-nine labors are nullified, for the world is sustained by His kindness, etc., as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above. (And see regarding this above in Hilchos Araiv, Halacha 3, where this matter is explained well.)</p>

<p>And therefore he revealed to them that the rectification of the labor of the field, to nullify the impurity of the serpent through which the ground was cursed &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;by the sweat of your brow you shall eat bread,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; and to nullify all of this, depends on the illumination of the Ratzon, as is explained above in Hilchos Araiv &mdash; see there. And all of this depends on Yosef, who is the aspect of the Ratzon of the R&rsquo;tzonos, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the second dream: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And behold, the sun and the moon and eleven stars were bowing down to me&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Beraishis 37:9)</span>. The sun and the moon and the eleven stars bowing down to Yosef HaTzaddik, who is the aspect of ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin, as above &mdash; this is the aspect of the nullification of nature. For the entire wisdom of nature is according to the arrangement of the constellations, according to the movements of the celestial spheres of the sun and the moon and the stars. And as Rabbainu of blessed memory wrote there in the Torah teaching mentioned above, on the verse: <span class="verse">&ldquo;They placed their signs as signs&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Tehillim 74:4)</span> &mdash; who say that everything is through the signs of heaven, G&ndash;d forbid, which is the nature. But in truth, everything is through His will alone, blessed be He, and nature itself is conducted only by His will alone, blessed be He. And &ldquo;He does as He pleases with the host of heaven and earth.&rdquo; For the sun and the moon and the stars, from which nature is drawn, all are conducted only by the Supernal Ratzon, from which is the root of Yosef, as above &mdash; the aspect of: &ldquo;and behold, the sun and the moon and eleven stars were bowing down to me.&rdquo; For nature is conducted only by the Supernal Ratzon, which is the aspect of ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin, from which is the root of the soul of Yosef HaTzaddik, as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;12</div>

<p>And all the guardians cannot guard properly except through emunas haratzon. For: <span class="verse">&ldquo;If Hashem does not guard the city, the watchman watches in vain&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Tehillim 127:1)</span>. For the essential guarding from the damaging forces of the world is through the revelation of the Ratzon, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore the Avos [forefathers] of the world were guardians and shepherds of sheep. For they needed to reveal the emunah in the world, which is the revelation of the Ratzon &mdash; to believe that everything is only by His will, blessed be He, and there is no nature at all. Therefore they were guardians &mdash; for they drew the guarding from its root, which is the holy emunah, which is the aspect of &ldquo;guard&rdquo; [shamor]. For at the time of their guarding, they connected their ratzon to the Supernal Ratzon, from which is the guarding, as above. And through this they drew and revealed emunas haratzon in the world.</p>

<p>And therefore the episode of Dovid HaMelech with the lion and the bear &mdash; which are the evil beasts, the aspect of the sages of nature, as is explained well in the Torah teaching mentioned above &mdash; was during the tending of the sheep, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Your servant was a shepherd,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;and the lion came, and the bear, and carried one from the flock,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Shmuel I 17:34)</span>. For it is all one. For during the tending of his sheep and his guarding of them &mdash; when he was engaged in drawing the revelation of the Ratzon in the world, as above &mdash; then the lion and the bear came, etc. And just as the lion and the bear came physically, so too they came upon him from their root &mdash; which are the evil beasts, which are the heresies of the sages of nature. And Dovid HaMelech, peace be upon him, was mighty and a man of valor, and he stood against them physically and spiritually, and he subdued and struck the evil beasts, which are the heresies, and nullified them spiritually at their root. And physically he prevailed and struck and killed the lion and the bear, through nullifying the power of their strength to harm.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of what Yaakov Avinu sent Yosef HaTzaddik to his brothers at the time they were shepherding, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Are not your brothers shepherding in Sh&rsquo;chem? Come, and I will send you to them&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Beraishis 37:13)</span>. That is, as above &mdash; for since your brothers are shepherding in Sh&rsquo;chem, and their entire labor is to draw the revelation of the Ratzon in the world &mdash; therefore &ldquo;come, and I will send you to them.&rdquo; For it is impossible for them to draw the revelation of the Ratzon except through Yosef HaTzaddik, who is the aspect of ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin &mdash; where all the r&rsquo;tzonos are connected. And through this is the essential revelation of the Ratzon, as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;13</div>

<p>And the Sh&rsquo;vatim, who blemished Yosef &mdash; who is the aspect of the revelation of the Ratzon, as above &mdash; therefore it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And we will say: An evil beast devoured him,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Beraishis 37:20)</span>. And likewise Yaakov said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;An evil beast devoured him; torn, torn is Yosef&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Beraishis 37:33)</span>. This is the aspect of the evil beasts that maul and tear, which are the aspect of the sages of nature who blemish the Ratzon, which is the aspect of Yosef, as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above.</p>

<p>And behold, the Evil One incited them then and wanted to induce them to kill Yosef entirely. For the Evil One wants to blemish and deny the root of the Ratzon entirely, G&ndash;d forbid. But Hashem, blessed be He, had compassion upon them and upon the world at large, and arranged in His mercy that they did not kill him entirely, but only sold him for money to Egypt.</p>

<p>That is, as above &mdash; for they blemished only in the aspect of theft and loss. For they stole him and sold him, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;For I was stolen, stolen from the land of the Hebrews,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Beraishis 40:15)</span>. That is, the blemish of the Ratzon, the aspect of Yosef, was only in the aspect of theft &mdash; which is the aspect of the blemish drawn through the evil beasts, who are the sages of nature for their own pleasure, who introduce error into the heart of a person through theft and distraction. And this is the aspect of: &ldquo;and the lion and the bear came, and carried one from the flock&rdquo; &mdash; that he carried one from the flock, who denied the Ratzon, as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above. But it was in the manner of theft, like one who carries a sheep from the physical flock by theft. But they did not kill Yosef entirely &mdash; which is the aspect of murderers and robbers, who are in the aspect of the forehead of the serpent, the aspect of unavoidable circumstances.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;14</div>

<p>And therefore the paid guardian is liable for theft and loss and is exempt from unavoidable circumstances, and the borrower is liable even for unavoidable circumstances. For the money and the possessions of every person are drawn from the root of the Supernal Ratzon, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You open Your hand and satisfy every living thing with ratzon&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Tehillim 145:16)</span>. And as is explained and understood in the Torah teaching mentioned above &mdash; that through the revelation of the Ratzon one merits the abundance of sustenance without any labor at all. It emerges that all money and sustenance are drawn through the revelation of the Ratzon. And therefore the Ratzon is clothed in the money and the possessions, the aspect of: &ldquo;and satisfy every living thing with ratzon,&rdquo; as above.</p>

<p>And this is what is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Naftali is satisfied with ratzon and full of the blessing of Hashem&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Devarim 33:23)</span>. For the wealth and the sustenance are the aspect of the illumination of the Ratzon. And this is what our Sages of blessed memory said: &ldquo;After the master of possessions, drag the beam&rdquo; [basar marai nichsay tzivay mashuch]. For everyone is drawn after the ratzon of the wealthy person, because money at its root is drawn from the illumination of the Ratzon.</p>

<p>And this owner of the house, whose money and vessels are his &mdash; with him is the aspect of the root of the Ratzon that is clothed in the money. For he can do with it as he desires and wishes, as his heart desires. And therefore it is incumbent upon him to connect the ratzon that is in the money to the root of the Supernal Ratzon &mdash; by subjugating all the money to Hashem, blessed be He, to conduct himself with the money only according to His will, blessed be He, to do with it tzedakah and mitzvos. And through this the money is guarded from all damages. For the essential guarding is through the illumination of the Ratzon, which is drawn through tzedakah, by connecting the money to His will, blessed be He, as above. For just as one connects himself &mdash; his body and his soul and his money &mdash; to His will, blessed be He, so too the Supernal Ratzon is drawn upon him, and through this he is guarded from all evil.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;15</div>

<p>And therefore all the craftsmen are paid guardians [shomrai sachar]. For all craftsmanship is drawn from the aspect of the thirty-nine labors, which correspond to the thirty-nine labors of the Mishkan [Tabernacle]. And when one merits the illumination of the Ratzon through tzedakah &mdash; through which the revelation of the root of the Ratzon is rectified &mdash; then all the labors are nullified entirely, for the world is sustained by His kindness, etc. But as long as one does not merit the revelation of the Ratzon in completeness, and the forehead of the serpent is not subdued at its root &mdash; rather one only connects all the r&rsquo;tzonos to the root of the Ratzon &mdash; then the labors are not yet completely nullified. Rather, through the connection of the Ratzon to the root of the Ratzon, through this one merits to do the labors in holiness, in the aspect of the labor of the Mishkan (and this matter is explained and understood well above in Hilchos Araiv).</p>

<p>And therefore the craftsmen are paid guardians. For the rectification of the craftsmen is in the aspect of the connection of the Ratzon to its root &mdash; through which they are guarded from theft and loss alone, not from unavoidable circumstances. For from unavoidable circumstances one is not saved except through the rectification of the root of the Ratzon itself &mdash; through which the craftsmanship and the labors are nullified entirely. But the craftsmen who are engaged in their craft and their labor &mdash; this is the aspect of the rectification of the labors through the connection of the r&rsquo;tzonos to their root, and they have not yet merited the rectification of the root of the Ratzon itself to remove from it the blemish of the heresy of the forehead of the serpent. For then the craftsmanship and the labors would be nullified entirely, as above. And therefore the responsibility for unavoidable circumstances is not upon them &mdash; for unavoidable circumstances are not nullified except through the subjugation of the forehead of the serpent, through which the root of the Ratzon is revealed. And they are liable only for the responsibility of theft and loss.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;16</div>

<p>And this is what is said regarding Aisav, who is the aspect of Amalek, the aspect of the root of the wisdom of nature <span class="inline-source">(Ovadyah 1:5)</span>: <span class="verse">&ldquo;If thieves came to you,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;How are you made silent,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;How are the things of Aisav searched out, his hidden things laid bare!&rdquo;</span></p>

<p>For in the future, the forehead of the serpent will be subdued and the forehead of the Ratzon will be revealed. And then the heresies of the sages of nature, who are the aspect of Aisav, will be nullified entirely. And this is: &ldquo;If thieves came to you,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; that is, they will no longer come with the sages of nature through theft. For now they sometimes come through theft and deceptions, as above &mdash; and one must conduct oneself against them also through theft, to incline the da&rsquo;as to emunas haratzon, to steal the souls that were ensnared by them in the net of their error, to incline them to the truth. For now it is impossible to go out against them with an upraised hand, because the forehead of the serpent has not yet been subdued at its root entirely.</p>

<p>But in the future, when the forehead of the serpent will be completely subdued and the root of the Ratzon will be revealed &mdash; then it will be fulfilled: &ldquo;How are the things of Aisav searched out, his hidden things laid bare!&rdquo; For all the hidden things of his wickedness and his heresy will be revealed. For they will be able to subdue him openly, with an upraised hand &mdash; for emunas haratzon will be revealed to the eyes of all.</p>

<p>And then it will be fulfilled: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And saviors shall ascend upon Mount Tzion, to judge the mount of Aisav; and the kingship shall be Hashem&rsquo;s&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Ovadyah 1:21)</span>. For everyone will accept the yoke of His kingship, blessed be He, in love. For it will be revealed to all who come into the world that everything is according to His will, blessed be He, alone &mdash; for Hashem is G&ndash;d, there is nothing else besides Him. Blessed be Hashem forever. Amain v&rsquo;amain.</p>

